  "notes": "The individual exterior includes a pale rockfill slope, continuous crest road and rails, open circular overflow, thick weir rim, bank retaining wall and service landing. A white tower with a red roof accompanies the gallery and slanted intake rails. The lower ochre powerhouse has a broad red gabled roof, two auxiliary buildings, outfall walls, transformers and a simplified switchyard. The sampled reservoir is 9.65 m above the operator’s maximum operating pool and submerges the spillway rim. Coarse native shoreline-bank geometry also intersects part of the lower hall and service gallery. These site-fit issues keep geographic and medium-fi acceptance pending. Rockfill sections, foundations, intake rails, lower plant layout and equipment are exterior approximations. Gates and water are static; internal machinery and buried conduits are outside this model.",
